{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"073946d02266f015e07012e50eb5680ee2de1432922ba0a4ed603c8740e646d3","packTokens":6730,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"platform","tokens":215,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":1,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":4190,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":2219,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"PLATFORM. This product is designed and built as a web app, and nothing else. Where the requirements ask for a mobile app, a phone app, an iOS or Android app, treat them as the same features in one responsive web app that works well on a phone's browser: never stop, park, ask or leave a requirement out because it names a mobile app, and never plan a native app, an app store step or a phone-only frame. Every page is responsive: it is laid out for a phone, a tablet and a desktop width, with touch-sized controls on the narrow one. What only a native app can do (push notifications, background location, a home-screen icon) is given its closest web form (an in-app notice or email, the browser's location prompt, an installable web app) and said so.\n\nMap each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"How should users authenticate to the driver, staff, and customer areas?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use individual email-and-password accounts with self-service password reset.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Who can create, deactivate, and assign roles and access scopes to users, including a staff member’s warehouses and a customer user’s organisation?\",\n  \"answer\": \"A System Administrator manages accounts, roles, warehouse access, and customer-organisation access.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"For a customer’s recall response, may reported on-hand, used/dispensed, and destroyed quantities total less than the quantity delivered, leaving a remainder unaccounted?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Allow a smaller total; track the remainder as unaccounted until it is later accounted for or written off with a signed justification.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"How long must the handover signature and delivery photo remain available?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Retain them for seven years, matching the audit-record retention period.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"What existing records, if any, must be brought into the new system at launch so lot tracing and recall quantities work from the start?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Start with no imported records; enter opening lots and stock in the new app.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Who is authorized to sign a write-off of unaccounted recall quantities?\",\n  \"answer\": \"A Quality Manager.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"For a partial refusal, can the receiver refuse a quantity within a shipper box, or only accept/refuse whole boxes?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Record acceptance or refusal only for whole boxes, with a reason for each refused box.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"What tier limits, allowance budgets, and permitted temperature ranges should drive excursion recommendations, and are they shared or product-specific?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use one configured set of tier limits and allowances for all products.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Yes: \\\"The driver sees today's route with its stops in order.\\\"\",\n  \"by\": \"factory\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-17\",\n  \"question\": \"Does the request ask for this: Show drivers only their assigned routes for today, with each route’s stops in route order.\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Yes: \\\"Loading requires every box on the route to be scanned, and a wrong or missing box is reported.\\\"\",\n  \"by\": \"factory\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-18\",\n  \"question\": \"Does the request ask for this: Compare scanned shipper boxes with expected boxes before departure, report missing or wrong-route boxes, and block departure until every expected box is scanned and wrong boxes are removed or corrected.\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Yes: \\\"The dispatcher sees each stop's status and the time it was last updated.\\\"\",\n  \"by\": \"factory\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-19\",\n  \"question\": \"Does the request ask for this: Show dispatchers each route stop’s status and last-updated time.\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Yes: \\\"During the route the application shows the current temperature and status of each box and any alerts.\\\"\",\n  \"by\": \"factory\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-20\",\n  \"question\": \"Does the request ask for this: Show each route box’s latest available temperature, status, and gateway alerts, and mark cached temperature data as stale while disconnected.\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Yes: \\\"If a box holds stock that is On Hold, the application shows \\\"Do not deliver\\\" for that box and does not allow it to be handed over.\\\"\",\n  \"by\": \"factory\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-21\",\n  \"question\": \"Does the request ask for this: For scanned boxes on hold, display “Do not deliver” and the returned hold reason, and prevent handover of those boxes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Yes: \\\"For the remaining boxes, the driver records the receiver's name, captures their signature and a photo of the delivered boxes, and completes the handover. The time and location are recorded automatically.\\\"\",\n  \"by\": \"factory\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-22\",\n  \"question\": \"Does the request ask for this: Let drivers record eligible handovers with receiver name, signature, delivery photo, actual handover time, and available browser location.\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Yes: \\\"If the route was changed while the driver was offline, the driver is shown the difference before continuing, and a handover already completed offline is never lost or undone.\\\"\",\n  \"by\": \"factory\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-23\",\n  \"question\": \"Does the request ask for this: When an assigned route changes while a driver is offline, show route differences, require review and resolution of affected unsent work before continuing, and preserve completed offline handovers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Yes: \\\"The system shows the reviewer the full temperature history, the budget used and remaining per tier, and a recommendation: Release when every tier still has allowance left, Reject when any tier is used up or a not-permitted range was reached.\\\"\",\n  \"by\": \"factory\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-24\",\n  \"question\": \"Does the request ask for this: Present a single-person quality-decision flow only when an excursion is within the first tier above or below the permitted band, allowance remains, and the proposed decision matches the recommendation. Otherwise require a Quality Officer proposal and separate approval by a different Quality Manager. Require written justification when a decision opposes the recommendation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Yes: \\\"Each decision is signed electronically: the person confirms their identity again at the moment of signing and gives a reason. A signed decision cannot be edited. It can only be superseded by a new signed decision, and both remain on record.\\\"\",\n  \"by\": \"factory\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-25\",\n  \"question\": \"Does the request ask for this: Require identity confirmation using the account’s sign-in method and a reason when a user signs a quality decision; present signed decisions as read-only with a separate superseding-decision action.\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Yes: \\\"If the excursion stayed within the first tier above or below the band and allowance remains, a Quality Officer may decide alone.\\\"\",\n  \"by\": \"factory\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-26\",\n  \"question\": \"Does the request ask for this: When the service returns a quality disposition, show resulting stock, order, and route status and, when superseded, the earlier and current disposition.\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Yes: \\\"Destruction is recorded with a date, a quantity and a witness.\\\"\",\n  \"by\": \"factory\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-27\",\n  \"question\": \"Does the request ask for this: Collect destruction date, quantity, and witness for rejected stock, and prevent entry of a quantity greater than the displayed rejected quantity.\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Yes: \\\"Decisions waiting longer than 4 hours are escalated to the Quality Manager.\\\"\",\n  \"by\": \"factory\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-28\",\n  \"question\": \"Does the request ask for this: Identify decisions waiting more than four hours as escalated in the Quality Manager’s waiting-decisions view.\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Yes: \\\"A Quality Manager starts a recall for a product and one or more lot numbers, with a reason and a severity.\\\"\",\n  \"by\": \"factory\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-29\",\n  \"question\": \"Does the request ask for this: Provide a Quality Manager flow to start and close recalls with signed actions; recall start collects product, one or more lots, reason, and severity, and the app displays each returned action result.\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Yes: \\\"The trace from lot to every location and customer shall be available within one minute of the request.\\\"\",\n  \"by\": \"factory\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-30\",\n  \"question\": \"Does the request ask for this: Display the returned recall trace, including warehouse locations, boxes, routes, customer deliveries, quantities, delivery dates, receivers, and the trace total alongside received quantity when supplied.\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Yes: \\\"Notifies those customers by email and in the customer portal.\\\"\",\n  \"by\": \"factory\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-31\",\n  \"question\": \"Does the request ask for this: Show customer recall notices in the portal, link notices to affected deliveries, and provide a response entry point.\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Yes: \\\"The customer portal shows the organisation's orders, their status, the lots and expiry dates allocated, and for deliveries on the road the planned arrival time and whether the temperature is in range.\\\"\",\n  \"by\": \"factory\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-32\",\n  \"question\": \"Does the request ask for this: Show customers only their organisation’s current and past orders, allocated lots and expiry dates, order status, and in-transit delivery arrival and temperature status, without exposing other route customers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Yes: \\\"After delivery, the customer can download a delivery certificate as a PDF for each delivery.\\\"\",\n  \"by\": \"factory\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-33\",\n  \"question\": \"Does the request ask for this: Provide a PDF certificate for each completed delivery in the signed-in customer’s organisation, containing products, lots, expiry dates, quantities, receiver, handover time, each box’s temperature chart from sealing to handover, excursions, and signed excursion decisions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Yes: \\\"Each affected customer responds in the portal with, for each delivery, how many packs are still on hand, how many were used or dispensed, and how many were destroyed on site.\\\"\",\n  \"by\": \"factory\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-34\",\n  \"question\": \"Does the request ask for this: When late readings produce a new certificate version, list the new and earlier versions for the signed-in customer’s completed delivery and keep each available for download.\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Yes: \\\"Recall progress shows the percentage of packs accounted for.\\\"\",\n  \"by\": \"factory\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-35\",\n  \"question\": \"Does the request ask for this: Present the customer portal and certificates in the user’s selected English or Arabic, render Arabic right to left including tables and charts, and show dates and times in the account’s configured time zone.\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Yes: \\\"A customer sees current and past orders of their own organisation only.\\\"\",\n  \"by\": \"factory\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-36\",\n  \"question\": \"Does the request ask for this: Provide an audit-trail screen showing returned entries with actor, time, changed fields, old and new values, and supplied reason; support filters by record, user, date range, and action type, and export the filtered view.\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Yes: \\\"The certificate contains the contents by lot, the handover details, the temperature chart, and any excursions with their decisions.\\\"\",\n  \"by\": \"factory\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-37\",\n  \"question\": \"Does the request ask for this: Show the returned history of a lot from receipt through delivery or destruction in time order.\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Yes: \\\"The same figures shall be available on screen for any date range, filterable by warehouse.\\\"\",\n  \"by\": \"factory\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-38\",\n  \"question\": \"Does the request ask for this: Provide on-screen reports for selected date ranges and warehouses, with CSV export of displayed figures, covering excursion counts and rates by route, driver, vehicle, and shipper box type; packs rejected and destroyed by product and cause; on-time deliveries within 60 minutes of planned arrival and in-full deliveries when every ordered pack is handed over, each as a percentage; average time from excursion to decision; stock within 60 days of expiry by product and warehouse; and open recalls and their progress.\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Yes: \\\"The portal and the certificate are available in English and Arabic according to the user's preference.\\\"\",\n  \"by\": \"factory\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-39\",\n  \"question\": \"Does the request ask for this: Make the web app responsive on phone, tablet, and desktop browsers, with touch-sized controls on narrow screens.\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Yes: \\\"The trace lists every warehouse location, box, route and customer delivery for the lot, with quantities.\\\"\",\n  \"by\": \"factory\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-40\",\n  \"question\": \"Does the request ask for this: Render the full recall trace returned by the service for the assumed launch scale.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-9\",\n  \"question\": \"Should this 34-requirement scope be approved as one run, split into multiple runs, or reduced?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Split the work into about three runs without cutting requirements.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-10\",\n  \"question\": \"If a driver's session expires while the browser is offline, may the driver continue recording loading, handover, and refusal work?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Allow local recording after expiry, but require the driver to re-authenticate before queued work can sync.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-11\",\n  \"question\": \"Should recall blocking and conflict handling extend to offline cached recall information, or apply only once the service is reachable? The request separately requires retaining and flagging an offline handover that conflicts with a hold.\",\n  \"answer\": \"Apply recall blocks from the service while online; do not add offline-cache recall blocking or a separate recall-conflict quality-case flow.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-12\",\n  \"question\": \"If the browser denies or cannot provide location, should an otherwise eligible handover still be allowed?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Allow the handover and record the location as unavailable.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-13\",\n  \"question\": \"Should the offline queue include safeguards beyond the requested local work retention and automatic sending, such as account isolation, re-authentication, retry identifiers, and review of permanently rejected payloads?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Keep the requested offline queue and automatic sending, without adding the extra account-isolation and rejected-payload review rules.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-14\",\n  \"question\": \"Should the web app have a formal browser support requirement for the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Do not add a fixed browser-version support requirement.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-15\",\n  \"question\": \"Should WCAG 2.1 AA conformance be added as an acceptance requirement for the main flows?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Do not add a formal WCAG 2.1 AA requirement.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-16\",\n  \"question\": \"Should a first-year product scale target be defined in this scope, in addition to the requested one-minute lot-trace availability?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Do not add a first-year product scale target; retain the explicitly requested lot-trace timing.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Provide the Meridian responsive web app with individual email-and-password sign-in and self-service password reset for driver, staff, and customer areas.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Provide System Administrator screens to create and deactivate accounts and assign roles, staff warehouse access, and customer-organisation access.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Show drivers only their assigned routes for today, with each route’s stops in route order.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Compare scanned shipper boxes with expected boxes before departure, report missing or wrong-route boxes, and keep departure blocked until all expected boxes are scanned and wrong boxes are removed or corrected.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Show dispatchers each route stop’s status and last-updated time.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Show each route box’s latest available temperature, status, and alerts from gateway data, and mark cached temperature data as stale while disconnected.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"For boxes with On Hold stock status, display “Do not deliver” and the returned hold reason, and prevent handover; allow handover only for deliverable boxes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"When online service data reports a scanned box as Recalled, display “Do not deliver” and prevent handover of that box.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Let drivers record eligible handovers with receiver name, signature, delivery photo, actual handover time, and available browser location.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"If browser location is denied or unavailable, allow an otherwise eligible handover and record location as unavailable.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Let drivers record full or partial refusals only by whole box, require a reason for each refused box, and display returned refusal and quarantine statuses.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"While offline, retain loading, handover, and refusal work locally across session expiry or sign-out; allow work to be recorded after expiry; require re-authentication before queued work syncs; automatically send queued work when connectivity returns; preserve handover occurrence time and identifier on retries; clear queued payload only after successful service acknowledgement; and show a storage error without reporting work as queued if local storage cannot retain the complete payload.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"When an assigned route changes while a driver is offline, show route differences, require review and resolution of affected unsent work before continuing, and preserve completed offline handovers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"When an offline handover conflicts with an On Hold status upon synchronization, retain and flag the handover and display the returned quality-case result.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"Show Quality reviewers the full excursion temperature history, allowance used and remaining for each tier, and the returned recommendation, using configured tier rules.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"Present a single-person quality-decision flow only when an excursion is within the first tier above or below the permitted band, allowance remains, and the proposed decision matches the recommendation; otherwise require a Quality Officer proposal and separate approval by a different Quality Manager. Require written justification when a decision opposes the recommendation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"Require identity confirmation using the account’s sign-in method and a reason when a user signs a quality decision; show signed decisions as read-only with a separate superseding-decision action.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"When the service returns a quality disposition, show resulting stock, order, and route status and, when superseded, the earlier and current disposition.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"Collect destruction date, quantity, and witness for rejected stock, and prevent entry of a quantity greater than the displayed rejected quantity.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"Identify quality decisions waiting more than four hours as escalated in the Quality Manager’s waiting-decisions view.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"Provide a Quality Manager flow to start and close recalls with signed actions; collect product, one or more lots, reason, and severity for recall start, and display each returned action result.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"Display the returned recall trace, including warehouse locations, boxes, routes, customer deliveries, quantities, delivery dates, receivers, and the trace total alongside received quantity when supplied.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 23,\n  \"text\": \"Show customer recall notices in the portal, link notices to affected deliveries, and provide a response entry point.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 24,\n  \"text\": \"Let customers submit or update per-delivery on-hand, used or dispensed, and destroyed quantities; allow a total below the delivered amount as unaccounted, and reject a total above it.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 25,\n  \"text\": \"Show recall progress as the returned percentage accounted for, identify outstanding customers and reminder status when supplied, and let a Quality Manager submit a signed write-off justification for unaccounted quantity.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 26,\n  \"text\": \"Show customers only their organisation’s current and past orders, allocated lots and expiry dates, order status, and in-transit delivery arrival and temperature status, without exposing other route customers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 27,\n  \"text\": \"Provide a PDF certificate for each completed delivery in the signed-in customer’s organisation, containing products, lots, expiry dates, quantities, receiver, handover time, each box’s temperature chart from sealing to handover, excursions, and signed excursion decisions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 28,\n  \"text\": \"When late readings produce a new certificate version, list the new and earlier versions for the signed-in customer’s completed delivery and keep each available for download.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 29,\n  \"text\": \"Present the customer portal and certificates in the user’s selected English or Arabic, render Arabic right to left including tables and charts, and show dates and times in the account’s configured time zone.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 30,\n  \"text\": \"Provide an audit-trail screen showing returned entries with actor, time, changed fields, old and new values, and supplied reason, with filters by record, user, date range, and action type and export of the filtered view.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 31,\n  \"text\": \"Show the returned history of a lot from receipt through delivery or destruction in time order.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 32,\n  \"text\": \"Provide on-screen reports for selected date ranges and warehouses, with CSV export of displayed figures, including excursion counts and rates by route, driver, vehicle, and shipper box type; packs rejected and destroyed by product and cause; deliveries on time within 60 minutes of planned arrival and in full when every ordered pack is handed over, each as a percentage; average time from excursion to decision; stock within 60 days of expiry by product and warehouse; and open recalls and their progress.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 33,\n  \"text\": \"Provide forms to enter opening lots and stock records and submit them to the service.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 34,\n  \"text\": \"Make recorded handover signatures and delivery photos available from a delivery record within its seven-year evidence-retention period.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 35,\n  \"text\": \"Make the web app responsive on phone, tablet, and desktop browsers, with touch-sized controls on narrow screens.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 36,\n  \"text\": \"Render the full recall trace returned by the service within 60 seconds after response receipt.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 37,\n  \"text\": \"Make the complete returned lot trace available through the client screen within 60 seconds of the user’s request.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}